    "updated_at": "2026-11-14T15:47:39Z",
    "body": "Readers of facet normals (the check that \"Done means\" asks for):\n\n- `crates/motion/src/finishing3d/pencil.rs` and `deburr.rs` use the facet winding to tell a concave edge from a convex edge. An inward closed body swaps the two. Then pencil can trace convex edges and deburr can select concave corners. I did not find a gouge path from this, and I did not examine the heights.\n- `geodesic.rs` lifts centers along vertex normals. It accepts only an open mesh. Its clearance check refuses a center on the wrong side, so the result is fewer contours, not a gouge.\n- `ladder.rs`, `support.rs`, `multiaxis/axis.rs` and `drilling/recognize.rs` use the absolute value or a folded sign. The winding does not change their result.\n\nWith PR #1671, a closed STEP body is outward before an operation reads it. An inward STL or OBJ body can still reach pencil and deburr. PR #1671 does not change STL or OBJ import.\n",
